{
  "name": "TestAssertEqualsOmitsMessageWhenNotInStepText",
  "comment": "Drift case 2 — the load-bearing reason this branch exists.\n\nStep text `- assert %message% equals 'hello plang'` (test/Simple/Start.goal:6)\ncarries no custom error message. With os/system/modules/assert/module.notes.md\nsaying \"omit Message from parameters and from formal unless the step text names\na custom error message; Expected is taken from the step text literal\", the LLM\nshould emit:\nparameters: { Expected: 'hello plang', Actual: %message% }   (no Message key)\n\nPre-fix shape this test forbids:\nany Message parameter on assert.equals (when step text had no custom message)\n\nRead .pr requires copying to a .txt first because '.pr' MIME deserializes to a\nGoal object, defeating substring assertions. Copy → read as text → assert.\nCompanion C# tests in DriftCaseArtifactTests.cs do the structural check too.\n\nArchitect's 3-fresh-cache rule runs externally (see sibling drift case).",
  "step": [
    {
